          <tei:p>What profit is there in our blood when we go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? Shall it declare thy truth? Why then inquirest thou after our iniquities, and searchest after our sins? Surely there is not a just man upon earth that doeth good, and sinneth not! But thou, my Lord, art a merciful and gracious God, long-suffering and abundant in goodness and truth. </tei:p>
