        <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:selichot/penitential_fourth_day/al_gabbi">
          <tei:pb n="135" ed="1912" facs="https://archive.org/download/selichothdavidasher1912/page/n272_medium.jpg"/>
          <tei:p>The ploughers ploughed upon my back; they made long their furrows. For our soul is bowed down to the dust, our belly cleaveth unto the earth. Lord, how are they increased that trouble us, many are they that rise up against us. Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercy’s sake. </tei:p>
        </tei:div>
        <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:selichot/penitential_fourth_day/verses_after_al_gabbi">
